{
  "id": "COMPOUND:25409 - PROTEIN:6340",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Salidroside may interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through a series of target relationships. Specifically, Salidroside is directly linked to DMS-79, which in turn is a target of Albaflavenone and Pseudopterosin P. All three of these compounds are known to target the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, indicating a potential pathway through which Salidroside could influence this complex. The scores assigned to these relationships are consistent, suggesting a plausible biological connection. The mechanism likely involves the interaction of Salidroside with DMS-79, which then modulates the activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. This integrated evidence supports the hypothesis that Salidroside may act as a modulator of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact nature of this interaction.",
